Potential null pointer exception: `session.cwd` is accessed on line 965, but `session` could be undefined if `this.sessionManager.get(params.sessionId)` returns undefined. This would cause the abort call to fail with a runtime error. The cleanup should occur after verifying the session exists, or the session's cwd should be passed via params or obtained safely.
```suggestion
      const session = this.sessionManager.get(params.sessionId)
      if (!session) {
        log.warn("cancel called for unknown session", { sessionId: params.sessionId })
        // Best-effort cleanup even if the session is unknown
        this.cleanupSession(params.sessionId)
        return
      }
```

Calling dispose() at the start of init() will call state() to get the subscriptions array, then clear it. However, after clearing the array in dispose(), the subsequent calls to s.subscriptions.push() (lines 74-99) will push to the same cleared array that was already obtained at line 71. This works, but creates a subtle dependency on the state() function returning the same object reference. This pattern is fragile and could break if the state implementation changes.
```suggestion
    // Clean up any existing subscriptions to prevent duplicates on re-init
    dispose()
    const s = state()
```

